show

# Per-instance startup state (per-clone, not shared).
startup/.instance.json
startup/.ghcr-push-state.json
startup/.ci-last-run.xml
# The Nessie lane's summary and a failure's evidence: single slots, cleared every
# run; the evidence is moved under startup/ci-reports/ with the run's record.
startup/.ci-nessie-last.json
startup/.ci-nessie-evidence/
# Per-run CI records. Local to the box that ran them: dev and prod each write
# their own, so committing them would collide across boxes for no gain.
startup/ci-reports/

# Generated BAML router client (regenerate via baml-cli generate --from NessieAI/dmac_assistant/baml_src)
NessieAI/dmac_assistant/src/dmac_assistant/router/baml_client/
# Second generators.baml target (e2e judge client); Task 12 04-baml-setup bind-mounts it.
NessieAI/dmac_assistant/tools/e2e/baml_client/

# Local design specs + plans (working docs, not part of the public repo).
# Excluded level-by-level so a single file can be re-included below; git will not descend
# into a directory excluded outright, which makes a bare negation inside it a no-op.
docs/superpowers/*
!docs/superpowers/specs/
docs/superpowers/specs/*
# Exceptions: the live CI coverage spec and the Nessie lane spec are tracked, because code
# cites them. The repo is PUBLIC, so they carry no environment concretes and no reproduction
# detail for any unresolved issue.
!docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-01-nextseek-ci-comprehensive-coverage-design.md
!docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-11-nessie-ci-lane-design.md
# Exception: the association-workbench design, cited by seek/views/admin.py and by the
# workbench CSS block in themes/NextSeek/static/css/nextseek.css. Same public-repo review
# applied: no environment concretes, no credentials, no unresolved-issue reproduction.
!docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-10-assay-association-workbench-design.md
!docs/superpowers/plans/
docs/superpowers/plans/*
# Exception: the implementation plan for the Nessie lane spec is tracked alongside it, so the
# design and the work it implies travel together. Same public-repo review applied: no
# environment concretes, no credentials, no reproduction detail for any unresolved issue.
!docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-11-nessie-ci-lane.md
# Exception: the association-workbench plan, tracked alongside its design for the same
# reason. Same public-repo review applied.
!docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-10-assay-association-workbench.md

# SEEK filestore: too large for git (raw dir ~500MB; snapshot ~215MB, over
# GitHub's 100MB/file limit, and forks can't host LFS). The snapshot is hosted
# on S3 and downloaded on demand by the startup CLI. See startup/seed/README.md.
/filestore/
startup/seed/filestore.tar.gz

# Paired --bayesian run directories: manifests are ~800K and the artifacts/
# tree is ~325M per run. They are deliverables, not source, and a `git add -A`
# that swept one in would be very hard to undo.
nessie_bayes_*/
# Ad-hoc nessie harness output directories (for example nessie_out_routing_<date>/).
# Same reasoning: run output, not source.
nessie_out*/

# graphify knowledge-graph output: ~62MB per build, of which graph.json alone is
# ~29MB. Regenerable from the tree at any time (`/graphify . --update`), so it is
# a local index, not source, and a `git add -A` that swept it in would be hard
# to undo on a repo this widely forked.
graphify-out/

# Generated publication-transfer data, regenerable from the documented queries
docs/archive/2026-08/publication-rollout/sample_publication_attributes/prod_pairs.tsv
docs/archive/2026-08/publication-rollout/prod_publication_transfer/all_52_publications.sql

# CI credentials must never enter git (they live at ~/.config/nextseek/ci.env)
ci/**/*.env
ci.env

# Superpowers working state (brainstorm mockups, SDD ledgers) is local only. A finished
# ledger worth keeping is filed under docs/archive/<yyyy-mm>/ instead.
.superpowers/
